        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): dripping proxy SSE bodies cancel via outer abort",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes concern that an OpenClaw proxy LLM SSE body can keep dripping after headers and reset per-chunk idle forever. Total stream lifetime must stay owned by the configured outer agent/provider abort budget (`signal`), not a hidden proxy-local ceiling.\n\nAffected workflow: `streamProxy` (`/api/stream` SSE) when agents route model calls through a proxy server.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`streamProxy` already bounds pre-header waits and per-chunk SSE idle (default 120s). After headers, the pre-header abort is intentionally cleared so `timeoutMs` is not an absolute stream deadline (#97235). Idle alone resets on every chunk.\n\nClawSweeper rejected an unconditional one-hour proxy-local default (`merge-risk: compatibility`) because whole-run budgets can exceed 1h. This revision:\n\n1. Keeps total lifetime owned by `options.signal` / outer abort by default — **no proxy-local default ceiling**.\n2. Keeps `streamDeadlineMs` as an **opt-in only** escape hatch for callers who explicitly want a proxy-local wall-clock.\n3. Arms that opt-in deadline only after the response reader exists so `cancel()` can interrupt a drip.\n4. Adds native loopback `/api/stream` proof for both outer abort and explicit `streamDeadlineMs`.\n\nNon-goals: making pre-header `timeoutMs` an absolute stream deadline again; documenting a new one-hour product contract; live proxy provider auth.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDripping keepalive-style proxy SSE bodies are canceled when the outer abort fires, without cutting off healthy streams that are still within a longer configured agent/provider budget. Callers that explicitly pass `streamDeadlineMs` get a bounded proxy-local wall-clock; everyone else keeps the prior lifetime ownership model.\n\n## Evidence\n\nHead: `7a5e2b27281`\n\n### Exact commands\n\n```bash\nOPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/runtime/proxy.test.ts\n```\n\n### Focused tests (16 passed)\n\n```text\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.9 /home/princeht/fire_project/openclaw-wt-109185\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  16 passed (16)\n   Duration  1.96s (transform 948ms, setup 602ms, import 372ms, tests 811ms, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 6.22s\n```\n\nIncludes:\n- existing “pre-header timeout is not an absolute stream deadline” regression still green\n- existing idle re-arm / idle stall regressions still green\n- fake-timer opt-in `streamDeadlineMs` drip case\n- **native loopback** `/api/stream` drip canceled by outer `AbortSignal` → `stopReason: \"aborted\"`, `Request aborted by user`, elapsed &lt; 1.5s\n- **native loopback** `/api/stream` drip canceled by explicit `streamDeadlineMs: 250` → wall-clock error inside budget\n\n### Autoreview\n\n```text\n.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode uncommitted --base origin/main --engine claude\n→ autoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported\n→ overall: patch is correct (0.95)\n```\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior addressed: dripping SSE after headers cannot outlive the outer abort; opt-in deadline also works on native fetch/ReadableStream\n- Environment: real Node `http` loopback on `127.0.0.1` + real `fetch` / SSE body (no mocked reader)\n- What was not tested: live remote proxy provider outage with provider credentials\n\n### Risk / Compatibility\n\nRemoves the previously proposed unconditional one-hour default. Opt-in `streamDeadlineMs` is local-only (not serialized to the proxy). AI-assisted.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
